# Loaded by `vite build` and by nothing else — Vite reads `.env.production`
# only in production mode, so `bun dev` and the Playwright suite never see it.
#
# COMMITTED ON PURPOSE, and it is the reason `bun run deploy` is safe to run by
# hand. `.env.production` outranks `.env` (Vite's own precedence: shell >
# `.env.production` > `.env.local` > `.env`), so the localhost address a
# developer keeps in `.env` for `bun dev` can no longer reach a production
# build. Before this file existed it could, and did: `todo/repo.md`'s REPO-09
# records a local `.env` that would have shipped a live site calling a laptop.
#
# Nothing here is a secret. `VITE_API_URL` is inlined into the browser bundle,
# so it is published to every visitor the moment the site deploys; the real
# secrets — the Sentry token, the PostHog key — stay in GitHub Actions and are
# read from the environment. Do not add one here.
#
# This is the ONLY place the deployed editor's API address is written down. CI
# used to restate it in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and no longer does, because
# two copies of an address that must never disagree is a way for them to
# disagree. `apps/editor/scripts/check-deployable-bundle.ts` reads this file
# and refuses the upload if the built bundle names anything else.

VITE_API_URL=https://api.agentsinc.sh
